  "hypothesis": "Five-slot tuning round 2 (DECISIONS #171). Round 1, replicated on its sealed holdout, measured a clean lever split: trim moved only the bulwark edge (-0.800 -> -0.600 pooled), drag moved only the striker edge (+0.667 -> +0.133 pooled) and stalled the fabricator mirror (9/10 capped), boom moved nothing. Round 2 registers the composites: moor (trim + drag) and wane (trim + a half-step 22-tick rebuild, the hedge against drag's mirror stall), plus a DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY column 'break' = the kit minus five slots per pair: shell alone on bulwark-vs-fabricator (if it lands near the keel anchor +0.056, the slots own the whole bulwark edge; near -0.5, the shell -- rule or doctrine mispricing -- owns the residual and no five-slot knob can close T2), volley alone on fabricator-vs-striker (attributing the fan's solo effect against the 0.000/+0.333 keel anchor), and the bare keel mirror as the pacing anchor. Gates: T1 the full control replicates round 1 pooled (bulwark-vs-fabricator within 0.25 of -0.800); T2 some composite brings both cross-class fabricator edges to |payoff| <= 0.40 ([0.15,0.40] aspirational; the striker-side edge remains population-capped by arc-light's -1.00-everywhere); T3 do-no-harm per composite: fabricator-mirror draw rate and capped share must not exceed the full arm's by more than 0.05 (drag's 9/10 cap is the registered failure mode), and pooled leader-extends not below 0.45x the control's. SELECTION RULE: adopt the composite minimizing max(|bvf|, |fvs|) among T3 passers; tie prefers moor (principled baseline-30 clock over the invented 22). break is never adoptable. If neither composite passes T2, adopt nothing and take the attribution to the owner: the next knob is the shell-vs-swarm question or slot 4, not a rebuild clock. Wave-4 doctrine/schedule disclosure carries over from round 1.",
